      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1902, Mont Alto State Forest Park became Pennsylvania’s first state forest park, later renamed Mont Alto State Park.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11,
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.pa.gov/agencies/dcnr/recreation/where-to-go/state-parks/find-a-park/mont-alto-state-park/history",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Conservation pioneer Joseph Rothrock warned that without reforestation, Pennsylvania’s highlands would wash into the ocean.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
